  "implementation": {
    "scope": "Shared stone and metal dressing across all five dungeon themes: vigil feet/shafts/cages, coffer bodies/lids/straps, fonts, waystones and existing metal/stone motifs. Existing colored light, emissive accents, ward, floors, walls, roots and gameplay unchanged.",
    "surface": "Seamless generated mineral grain/forge marks with independent sRGB albedo, tangent normal and linear roughness maps; mineral and tarnished metal colors remain readable under regional light. Smooth supplied geometry normals replace forced flat shading only on these two finishes.",
    "ownership": "Six maps/two existing materials per kit, shared by all rooms; kit/material disposal releases them. No global cache, per-room textures, animation clock, new material groups, geometry, lights, render passes, colliders or authoritative state.",
    "quality": "High128 andLow64 pixels for prop maps. Verdant retains its established256floor/wall maps on both qualities; elemental floors retainHigh256/Low64.",
    "cost": "Six added RGBA maps:384KiB raw CPU pixels High/96KiB Low per kit; approximately512KiB/128KiB for full RGBA8 mip chains, excluding driver overhead. Existing PBR shaders now sample albedo/normal/roughness. This adds shading/texture work; no FPS or broad performance improvement claimed."
  },
